{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Take for yourself from every food, etc.</b> 'For yourself' implies from your own, not from others' — in the manner of 'from yourselves' stated concerning the four species (Leviticus 23:40) — so that Noah should not reason: behold, today or tomorrow they will all die and their possessions will be destroyed, and you might suppose it is permitted to take from theirs. Therefore Scripture says 'take for yourself' — from your own specifically — to magnify the miracle: for although according to nature it would suffice only for you alone, since Noah certainly had no surpluses, nevertheless by way of miracle HaShem will send the blessing in your storehouses (Deuteronomy 28:8), and there will be for you and for them to eat. And likewise 'make for yourself an ark,' etc. — for in the natural course it would hold you alone, and by way of miracle it would hold all the living creatures, such as elephants and re'em."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:26.544377891Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}